<Axiom id="AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED">
      `FLOW_VERSION=v1` migration and runtime `EXECUTION_READY=no` remediation can dwarf a narrow request.
      Size only those broad actions to the task's own blast radius: a narrow owning spec edit may proceed
      without migrating unrelated legacy tasks or installing unrelated runtime gates. Each `AUTHORING_SCOPE`
      fact is different: it is a target-specific structural proof and is binding whenever scaffold would create
      tickets. A red authoring fact blocks scaffold but never blocks the named owning spec flow that repairs
      the evidence. Product execution always consumes `EXECUTION_READY`; only the exact active GATE_QUEUE
      setup phase receives its typed exemption.
    </Axiom>

